                "event": "Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Melbourne FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 14 at 9:34PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Lake and Volusia Counties.\n\n.The St Johns River at Astor is forecast to remain in Minor Flood\nStage through Friday, as previous heavy rainfall continues to drain\nthrough the basin. However, strong northeasterly winds are forecast\nthis weekend and will return the river to Moderate Flood Stage.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 3.0 feet, Water approaches or may enter lowest homes\non or near Wildhog Road and nearby canals. Flooding reaches the\nparking lot of the Juno Trail Apartments. Flooding on portions of\nAlligator Road and Holiday Road. Lowest lying yards along Blue\nCreek are flooded. Roads at Astor Landing Campground and Lake\nDexter Boat Ramp begin to flood. Water enters lower homes closest\nto the river on McPherson Lane.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:30 PM EDT Wednesday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 8:30 PM EDT Wednesday was 2.9 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 2.7 feet.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Thursday morning at 1100 AM EDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
