                "senderName": "NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 14 at 9:17PM EDT until October 17 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nFlorida...\n\nMyakka River At Myakka River State Park affecting Sarasota County.\n\n.Due to recent heavy rainfall, the water level along the Myakka River\nat Myakka River State Park remains elevated in Flood Stage.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Myakka River at Myakka River State Park.\n\n* WHEN...Until Saturday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 7.3 feet, Picnic areas and adjacent parking lots\nflood.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:00 PM EDT Wednesday the stage was 7.2 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 9:00 PM EDT Wednesday was 7.2 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 7.2 feet\njust after midnight tonight. It will then fall below flood stage\nearly Saturday afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 7.2\nfeet on 12/28/2002.\n- https://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Thursday morning at 1100 AM EDT.",
                "response": "Avoid",
